{
  "slug": "egg-white-fried-rice",
  "name": "Egg white fried rice",
  "description": "Cold cooked white rice tossed in a hot pan with plenty of egg white, broccoli, carrot, onion and garlic, sharpened with sriracha.",
  "iconKey": "bowl",
  "instructions": [
    "Heat the canola oil in a wok or wide skillet over high heat.",
    "Add the onion, carrot and broccoli and stir-fry until crisp-tender, about 4 minutes.",
    "Add the garlic, then the cooked white rice, and toss until the rice is hot and the grains separate.",
    "Push the rice to one side, pour in the egg white and stir until it just sets, then toss it back through the rice.",
    "Season with the salt and the sriracha and serve in two bowls."
